Z||000009||MinnGreenGT||07-31-2001||12:19 PM||||I believe that for the most part, front fascias are interchangable mounting wise. But the problem comes in with the trim. Different years used different style trim ('84-'85 have grooves, later models have smooth rounded trim). As for AUS's kit, check the General Fiero Forum- he's posting new info right now. Says the kit should be ready in about 3 weeks.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Hartz||07-31-2001||01:57 PM||||Yes, you could fit the front of the yellow car on your car.  The front of the yellow car (and the side, and the rear facial) are all standard Fiero parts.  You will have to get the underlaying honeycomb bumper, or seriously trim your coupe one, to fit, but otherwise it is a bolt on.  A Formula facia will also fit, and probably be a bit easier, as you won't need the underlaying honeycomb, or the side rocker panels and trim.<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>||||reg||1
